---
import ResourcesLayout from '../../layouts/ResourcesLayout.astro';

// Update whenever provider details on this page change.
const lastUpdated = 'September 2026';
---

<ResourcesLayout title="Internet Services" description="Available internet providers, typical speeds, and options for Crooked Lake Reserve" currentSection="internet-services">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
    <div class="bg-white p-8 rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-gray-100">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-6">
        <svg class="w-8 h-8 text-clr-orange" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M8.111 14.554a5 5 0 016.778 0M12 17h.01M3 15a9 9 0 0112-2.911M3 15a9 9 0 106.167 4.5" />
        </svg>
        <h1 class="text-3xl font-heading font-bold text-clr-green">Internet Services</h1>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 font-body -mt-4 mb-6">
        <strong>Last updated:</strong> {lastUpdated}
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-6">
        <p class="text-gray-700 font-body">
          Several internet options are available to Crooked Lake Reserve residents. Below is an overview of each service type, typical speeds, and links to check availability and sign up.
        </p>

        <!-- Fiber: Wire3 -->
        <div class="bg-clr-beige/30 border-2 border-clr-green rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8">
          <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-4 mb-4">
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
              <h2 class="text-xl font-heading font-bold text-clr-green">Wire3 (Fiber)</h2>
              <span class="inline-flex items-center bg-green-100 text-green-800 border border-green-300 px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold font-body">Now Available</span>
            </div>
            <a href="https://wire3.com/availability/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-clr-orange hover:brightness-110 text-white px-4 py-2 rounded-lg font-semibold text-sm shadow-md hover:shadow-lg transition-all font-body">
              Check Wire3 availability →
            </a>
          </div>
          <p class="text-gray-700 font-body mb-3">
            Wire3 fiber-optic internet is now available to all homes in Crooked Lake Reserve. Fiber delivers symmetrical upload and download speeds, low latency, and consistent performance—ideal for video calls, working from home, large uploads, and households with many devices. Wire3 is a Florida-based provider with no contracts, and plans include a Wi-Fi router.
          </p>
          <div class="bg-white/60 rounded-lg p-4 border border-gray-200">
            <strong class="text-clr-green">Typical speeds:</strong>
            <span class="text-gray-700 font-body"> Symmetrical plans from 250 Mbps up to multi-gigabit tiers. Check the Wire3 website for current plans and pricing at your address.</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Cable: Xfinity -->
        <div class="bg-clr-beige/30 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8">
          <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-4 mb-4">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-heading font-bold text-clr-green">Xfinity (Cable)</h2>
            <a href="https://www.xfinity.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-clr-orange hover:brightness-110 text-white px-4 py-2 rounded-lg font-semibold text-sm shadow-md hover:shadow-lg transition-all font-body">
              Visit Xfinity →
            </a>
          </div>
          <p class="text-gray-700 font-body mb-3">
            Xfinity delivers internet over the same coaxial cable used for TV. It is widely available in the area and offers a range of plans. Performance is generally consistent and suitable for streaming, work-from-home, and multiple devices.
          </p>
          <div class="bg-white/60 rounded-lg p-4 border border-gray-200">
            <strong class="text-clr-green">Typical speeds:</strong>
            <span class="text-gray-700 font-body"> Plan-dependent, from a few hundred Mbps on entry tiers up to gigabit and faster on higher tiers. Upload speeds are much lower than download speeds. Check the Xfinity website for current plans and pricing at your address.</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Cellular / 5G Home Internet -->
        <div class="bg-clr-beige/30 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-heading font-bold text-clr-green mb-4">Cellular Home Internet (5G / LTE)</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700 font-body mb-4">
            Major wireless carriers offer home internet over their cellular networks. A modem/router is installed at your home and uses the same network as cell phones. Availability and speeds depend on tower coverage at your address.
          </p>
          <div class="space-y-4">
            <div class="bg-white/60 rounded-lg p-4 border border-gray-200">
              <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2 mb-2">
                <strong class="text-clr-green">Verizon Home Internet</strong>
                <a href="https://www.verizon.com/internet" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-clr-orange hover:underline font-semibold text-sm">Check availability →</a>
              </div>
              <p class="text-gray-700 font-body text-sm">5G and LTE options. Typical speeds range from about 50 Mbps to 300+ Mbps where 5G is strong.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-white/60 rounded-lg p-4 border border-gray-200">
              <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2 mb-2">
                <strong class="text-clr-green">T-Mobile Home Internet</strong>
                <a href="https://www.t-mobile.com/home-internet" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-clr-orange hover:underline font-semibold text-sm">Check availability →</a>
              </div>
              <p class="text-gray-700 font-body text-sm">5G-based home internet. Speeds often in the 33–182+ Mbps range, varying by location.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-white/60 rounded-lg p-4 border border-gray-200">
              <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2 mb-2">
                <strong class="text-clr-green">AT&T Internet Air</strong>
                <a href="https://www.att.com/internet/internet-air/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-clr-orange hover:underline font-semibold text-sm">Check availability →</a>
              </div>
              <p class="text-gray-700 font-body text-sm">Wireless home internet over AT&T's cellular network (AT&T Fiber is not offered in our community). Speeds vary by location and signal strength.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Starlink -->
        <div class="bg-clr-beige/30 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8">
          <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-4 mb-4">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-heading font-bold text-clr-green">Starlink (Satellite)</h2>
            <a href="https://www.starlink.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-clr-orange hover:brightness-110 text-white px-4 py-2 rounded-lg font-semibold text-sm shadow-md hover:shadow-lg transition-all font-body">
              Visit Starlink →
            </a>
          </div>
          <p class="text-gray-700 font-body mb-3">
            Starlink provides internet via low-Earth-orbit satellites. It can be a good option where cable or fiber is limited. The dish needs a clear view of the sky to work properly.
          </p>
          <div class="bg-amber-50 border-2 border-amber-200 rounded-lg p-4 mb-3">
            <p class="text-amber-900 font-body text-sm">
              <strong>Antenna placement:</strong> For best performance and to comply with community guidelines, Starlink antennas should be mounted at the <strong>rear of the home</strong>, with a clear view of the sky. Contact the ARB if you have questions about placement before installing.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-white/60 rounded-lg p-4 border border-gray-200">
            <strong class="text-clr-green">Typical speeds:</strong>
            <span class="text-gray-700 font-body"> Often 50–200+ Mbps download; actual speeds vary with plan, obstructions, and network load. Latency is lower than traditional satellite internet.</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Choosing & Tips -->
        <div class="bg-white border-2 border-clr-green rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-heading font-bold text-clr-green mb-4">Choosing a Provider & Tips</h2>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-gray-700 font-body">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-clr-orange font-bold mt-1">•</span>
              <span><strong>Check your address:</strong> Use each provider's website to confirm availability and plan options at your specific address.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-clr-orange font-bold mt-1">•</span>
              <span><strong>Consider usage:</strong> Video calls, streaming, and work-from-home benefit from higher speeds and stable connections; cable and fiber usually offer the most consistent performance.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-clr-orange font-bold mt-1">•</span>
              <span><strong>Equipment placement:</strong> For Starlink, follow the rear-of-home guideline and ensure a clear view of the sky. For fiber, ask the installer where the exterior box and cable run will go before work begins. For cellular home internet, place the modem near a window or where signal is strongest.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
              <span class="text-clr-orange font-bold mt-1">•</span>
              <span><strong>ARB approval:</strong> Exterior equipment (e.g., Starlink dish, fixed wireless antennas) and any exterior changes from an installation must follow HOA guidelines and may require architectural review. Submit an ARB request before installing if you're unsure.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</ResourcesLayout>
